## 5. Technology Stack — Explained

| Technology | Why We Use It |
|---|---|
| **HTML/CSS/JS** | Standard web frontend — no framework needed for this scope |
| **Python Flask** | Lightweight, easy to learn, great for web apps with templates |
| **MySQL** | Robust relational DB, perfect for structured complaint data |
| **SQLAlchemy** | ORM to interact with MySQL using Python classes — no raw SQL needed |
| **Flask-Bcrypt** | Securely hash passwords — never store plain text |
| **Flask-Session** | Server-side session management for secure auth |
| **Flask-Migrate** | Database migration management |
| **Chart.js** | Beautiful, responsive charts for analytics dashboard |
| **Jinja2** | Flask's built-in templating engine — renders HTML from Python |
| **python-dotenv** | Manage secrets and config via `.env` file |

